# Direct runtime dependencies of the API and the Celery worker, with the
# minimum versions the code declares. Edit this file, not requirements.txt.
#
# requirements.txt is compiled from here and pins every package, transitive
# ones included, to an exact version. Render (both services) and CI install
# from requirements.txt only, so a deploy installs what was tested instead of
# whatever is newest on PyPI that day. Regenerate it from backend/ after any
# change here:
#
#   uv pip compile requirements.in --universal --python-version 3.12 -o requirements.txt
#
# Existing pins are kept unless you ask for a newer one with
# --upgrade-package NAME. The lock must install on 3.12 (CI, local venvs) and on
# 3.14.3, the version Render runs (PYTHON_VERSION in render.yaml).
